PalBeacon Sync npm package license notice

This package is a mixed-license distribution whose components remain under
their respective licenses:

- The palbeacon TypeScript command-line program is licensed under the
  MIT License. The full text is in dist/LICENSES/MIT.txt.
- The separate Linux x64 and Windows x64 Parser executables under dist/bin/
  are licensed under GPL-3.0-or-later because they integrate the palooz/ooz
  decoder. The full text is in dist/LICENSES/GPL-3.0-or-later.txt.
- Parser code derived from palhelm retains its Apache-2.0 notices. Other
  vendored components retain the licenses listed in
  dist/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and dist/LICENSES/.

The CLI does not link to the Parser. It launches the Parser as a child process
and exchanges JSON files. See dist/PARSER_SOURCE.md for the source repository,
exact source commit, decoder provenance, and build instructions corresponding
to the bundled executable.
